selftext:
I really like the survivor io gameplay, so I decided to vibecode my own, I decided to build it in r/swift SpriteKit since r/ClaudeAI Opus 4.8/5 (High/Max) is already pretty good at it. All assets were generated using r/OpenAI image-gen-2 with multiple sprite JSON files (example below) so I could algorithmically create variations of characters, mobs, tiles, and backgrounds. I've published non-game mobile apps before so once this game was done, I used [lance.app](http://lance.app) to automate the submission process end-to-end and now the game is live to play here:

[https://apps.apple.com/ro/app/domain-expansion-jjk-game/id6793254486](https://apps.apple.com/ro/app/domain-expansion-jjk-game/id6793254486)

Example JSON file: 

    {
      "anchors": {
        "jp_rabbit_f0": {
          "prompt": "A horned spirit rabbit enemy: round white-jade furred rabbit with a tiny jade horn on its forehead, long ears swept back, sprinting at full speed. Full body side view facing right, mid-stride with front and hind legs extended in a gallop. Strict limited palette: ivory white fur, pale jade accents, pink inner ears.",
          "height": 16
        },
        "jp_tortoise_f0": {
          "prompt": "A thorn-shell tortoise enemy: mossy green tortoise with jagged dark thorn spikes jutting from its shell, plodding steadily forward. Full body side view facing right, mid-stride with one front leg reaching forward and the opposite hind leg pushing back. Strict limited palette: moss green, dark pine green, earthy brown.",
          "height": 20
        },
        ......
      },
      "edits": {
        "jp_rabbit_f1": {
          "src": "jp_rabbit_f0",
          "instruction": "Sprint frame 2 of a 4-frame run cycle: all four legs gathered underneath the body, back slightly arched."
        },
        "jp_rabbit_f2": {
          "src": "jp_rabbit_f0",
          "instruction": "Sprint frame 3 of a 4-frame run cycle: legs stretched the opposite way, hind legs reaching forward under the body and front legs extended back, body low."
        },
        .......
      },
      "statics": {},
      "groups": {
        "jp_rabbit": {
          "frames": ["jp_rabbit_f0", "jp_rabbit_f1", "jp_rabbit_f2", "jp_rabbit_f3"],
          "height": 16
        },
        "jp_tortoise": {
          "frames": ["jp_tortoise_f0", "jp_tortoise_f1", "jp_tortoise_f2", "jp_tortoise_f3"],
          "height": 20
        },
        ......
      }
    }


I'm happy to answer any questions and I will appreciate any feedback!
